@startuml rvdroid_adaptive_strategy
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam useBetaStyle true

title RVDroid Adaptive Strategy Selection

|Current State Analysis|
start
:Analyze current UI state;
:Extract state characteristics;
note right: Form detection, complexity, etc.

|Context Analysis|
:Determine application context;
:Identify current task;
:Check exploration phase;

|Application Type|
if (Application type?) then (Authentication)
  :Prioritize login strategies;
  :Enable form completion capabilities;
  :Focus on security testing;
else if (E-commerce)
  :Prioritize product navigation;
  :Enable input generation for search;
  :Focus on transaction flows;
else if (Utility)
  :Prioritize feature discovery;
  :Enable systematic exploration;
  :Focus on functionality testing;
else (Other)
  :Use balanced approach;
endif

|Current Progress|
:Analyze coverage metrics;
:Calculate exploration progress;
:Check for exploration plateaus;

if (Coverage status?) then (Low overall coverage)
  :Prioritize breadth exploration;
  :Increase randomness factor;
else if (Good breadth, low depth)
  :Prioritize depth exploration;
  :Focus on complex interactions;
else if (Plateau detected)
  :Switch to alternative strategy;
  :Break out of local optimum;
else (Good coverage)
  :Focus on missed areas;
  :Refine exploration;
endif

|Memory Feedback|
:Consult memory system;
:Analyze past strategy performance;
:Identify most effective strategies;
:Calculate success rates;

|LLM Guidance|
if (LLM enabled?) then (yes)
  :Request LLM strategy recommendations;
  :Apply strategy directives;
endif

|Balancing|
:Calculate strategy weights;
:Apply dynamic weighting;
:Make final strategy selection;

:Return selected strategy;
stop

@enduml